 room  she hears christian moaning  she hears what she describes as a  struggle but she doesn't see it but she  hears it  and then she hears the moaning stomp and  then she sees dejuan ferguson  carry  a quiet christian and place him back in  bed  and then a short while later he comes  back in the room again  wraps him entirely in a blanket  and carries him out of the room  lynn ferguson never saw her brother  again after that  duane's defense attorneys argued to the  jury in their opening statement what  they say happened to their client's son  dejuan ferguson did not kill his son  in the early morning of june 11th of  2003  duan noticed that christian was sick  so when christian got sick  dejuan did what he normally did  which was to take christian to the  hospital  so he wrapped christian up in a blanket  because he was just in a t-shirt and a  diaper at the time  on the way to the hospital  dejuan realized he should have called  ahead when he realized his phone was out  of minutes  that's when he stopped at the pay phone  while at the pay phone dejuan left his  car running  and he realized his car was being stolen  as it sped away  dewan immediately got off the phone with  the hospital and called 9-1-1 to report  the car stolen  and that his disabled son was inside of  that vehicle  terry the prosecution said they filed  this case after a fresh set of eyes  reviewed it inconsistent stories from  ferguson and the fact that he stopped  cooperating did they do enough to start  proving their case in this opening  though  absolutely not they should have done far  more in the beginning listen the  prosecution has waited all these years  19 years 2003 was a long time ago and  granted there's nobody here it's hard to  prove a case if you don't have a body  but this was a nine-year-old boy it's  not like he went away on his own and  that story that someone stole the car is  bogus why do you have to stop at a pay  phone when you're going to the hospital  just go to the ho